  "body": "Would it be portent to add or adjust a certain tag in HTML5? Certainly, a element for injecting patched information into the page, like when facebook updates. This is usually very tedious. But if you had say a <inject> tag that JavaScript could render through applying to the document.inject[x] point, than you could have tables stretch, and ads update more and more easily as they are marked in the page. Document injection points are critical to modern pages which need constant refitting of information. And instead of adding and reloading a circumference of current and old information, than below the <inject> tag in should be rendered. A small patch of HTML5 or other script. If this is something that would increase the overall appeal, or simplify the language, than certainly it should be added. Thank you. -aunk\n",
